{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1780501966,"nonce":"nBM5Q2qx02el+hX+y7TG2S2gGZ4=","metadata":{"github-id":"UCE_lAHOK4fCvM8AAAABEMec_s7BFJQp"},"target":"0cba862ccef350d28992d1f8368980f0a867db4e3ee70580278ddc839a2e349d","message":"**Last on-water prep day before the June 4 freeze / class start.** At the Judd Gregg pier (saltwater, charted). M3 is the primary sonar (sidescan may appear before Massabesic, not this day).\n\n## Strategy — get a CLEAN survey run at last\nEvery recent deployment lost the clean-survey validation to buoy/CA firefights. The #205 wrap-up root-caused the line *swerving* to the AvoidanceController weaving along the **charted pier's S57 inflation gradient** ([nav#63](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_navigation/issues/63)) — a **pier/charted-water artifact that won't occur at Lake Massabesic (no S57 coverage)**.\n\nSo this day: **set `FollowPath.obstacle_avoidance_weight = 0` live on `controller_server`** to neutralize the avoider's path influence (and the whole CA firefight) → clean straight lines → finally validate the backlog below. Set it back afterward only if separately testing avoidance.\n\n## Must-do checklist (one boat day, weight=0)\n- [ ] **Mission re-send mid-line ([nav#35](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_navigation/issues/35) / PR #36)** — verify the fix takes effect on water. *Class-significant: students redirect mid-mission.*\n- [ ] **Mid-line resume after goto override ([nav#58](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_navigation/issues/58))** — characterize/validate (resume from current position, not line-restart). *Class-significant. May not have a fix yet — characterize at minimum.*\n- [ ] **Turning limits ([#124 §2](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/124))** — first real apron-turn validation of helm yaw 1.0 / planner radius 1.5 m.\n- [ ] **Cross-track / SE-undulation ([#164](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/164))** — first sustained clean survey line to characterize.\n- [ ] **OTH distance test ([#130](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/130))** — still untested.\n- [ ] **Smoother ±3.0 roll watch** — on a sharp yaw reversal, watch for hull roll (the #197/deployment-197 snap-roll risk re-opened by seafloor#38). Back off toward ±1.5 if it rolls.\n- [ ] **Command-logging verify ([#209](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/209))** — confirm `/bizzy/marine/command` + `/bizzy/piloting_mode/manual/helm` resolve on gabby so the boat recorder captures them.\n- [ ] **Operator logbook plugin ([unh_marine_autonomy#114](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_autonomy/issues/114))** — first on-water test of `rqt_operator_log`. It is **not wired into the operator launch**, so start it manually: add **Robot Tools → Operator Log** in rqt, or `ros2 run rqt_operator_log operator_log`. Enter a few notes during the run and confirm they record to the local `operator_log_*` rosbag2 (topic `/operator_logs`, `std_msgs/String`). *Goal: validate the human-notes-in-the-bag workflow before class so notes share the ROS timeline instead of a separate doc.*\n\n## Carry-forwards from #205\n- [ ] Offload the QINSy data.\n- [ ] Confirm M3 1PPS lock in the sonar console.\n\n## Notes\n- **Autonomous obstacle avoidance is fallback-only** with students (nav#63 swerving / nav#64 speed-limited CA) — not relied on.\n- TF extrapolation (nav#23) is **CLOSED/resolved** — not a watch item.\n- Predecessor: #205 (wrapped up via PR #208). Activate this day with `/start-deployment` (don't open a duplicate).\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null}]}